hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18210","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Said that is Ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Abu Aqil Zuhrah ibn Mabad al-Taymi narrated to me from his grandfather Abdullah ibn Hisham, and he had met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his mother Zaynab bint Humayd took him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, take his pledge. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is small. Then he wiped his head and supplicated for him, and he used to sacrifice one sheep for all his household."
"18211","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Ibn Luhayyah narrated to us from Zuhrah ibn Mabad from his grandfather, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was holding the hand of Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: By Allah, you, O Messenger of Allah, are dearer to me than everything except myself. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you believes until I am dearer to him than himself. Umar said: Then now, by Allah, you are dearer to me than myself. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Now, O Umar."
"22870","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Zuhrah, meaning Ibn Mabad ibn Abdullah ibn Hisham Abu Aqil, narrated to us, from his grandfather, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was holding the hand of Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him. So Umar said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, you are more beloved to me than everything except myself. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No, by the One in whose hand is my soul, until I am more beloved to you than yourself. Umar said: So you are now, by Allah, more beloved to me than myself. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Now, O Umar."
"22871","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Zuhrah Abu Aqil al-Qurashi narrated to us that his grandfather Abdullah ibn Hisham reached puberty in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and married women."
